      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "Toronto's offseason isn't a quiet recalibration - it's a full-throated reinvention, starting with the seismic arrival of No. 1 draft pick Gavin McKenna, whose hockey IQ \"is off the charts,\" per Dr. Hayley Wickenheiser. The Leafs, who finished 8th in the Atlantic with 78 points, are now star-hunting under GM John Chayka, who insists a GM's job is to \"star-hunt\" and isn't done yet. They've already added Sergei Bobrovsky between the pipes, Nick Paul down the middle, and depth forwards Jack Roslovic, Colton Sissons, and Brandon Duhaime - seven new players reshaping the roster. The move for Bobrovsky, a two-year, $10 million AAV, signals a goalie dominoes collapse the Leafs exploited. With McKenna potentially skipping No. 72 for Bobrovsky's legacy, the culture is shifting fast. <strong>The Leafs are stacking talent now, not waiting</strong> - and the next wave of signings could define their next decade.",
        "updated": "Updated July 3, 2026"
      },
