      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "The Toronto Blue Jays aren't just playing sloppy baseball - they're fighting to prove they belong in the contender conversation, and last night's explosion against New York was the loudest argument they've made yet. <strong>The Jays crushed the Mets 9-3 on July 1</strong>, snapping a two-game losing streak and injecting real energy into a 41-46 squad sitting 3rd in the AL East, 11.5 games behind the division lead. That win, part of a wild three-game Mets series where they split 2-1, highlights a team that can swing hot or cold in the same breath - exactly the mixed bag analysts are calling this season. Sal Stewart's electric homer off a 102.3 mph pitch is the kind of flash that keeps hope alive, even as injuries and inconsistency linger. Now, the real test begins: <strong>they head to Seattle Saturday at 10:10 PM ET to face the Mariners</strong>, a game that could define whether this team is rising or just rattling.",
        "updated": "Updated July 3, 2026"
      },
